  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "In right triangle \\(ABC,\\) \\(BC=5,\\) \\(AC=12,\\) and \\(AM=x;\\) \\(MN\\perp AC,\\) \\(NP\\perp BC;\\) \\(N\\) is on \\(\\overline{AB}.\\) If \\(y=MN+NP,\\) one-half the perimeter of rectangle \\(MCPN,\\) then:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(y=\\dfrac12(5+12)\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(y=\\dfrac{5x}{12}+\\dfrac{12}{5}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(y=\\dfrac{144-7x}{12}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(y=12\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(y=\\dfrac{5x}{12}+6\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "c",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1957-p37.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "By similarity, \\[ MN=\\frac5{12}AM=\\frac{5x}{12}. \\] Also \\(NP=MC=AC-AM\\) \\(=12-x.\\) Hence \\[ \\begin{aligned} y=MN+NP &=\\frac{5x}{12}+12-x\\\\ &=\\frac{144-7x}{12}. \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Triangles \\(AMN\\) and \\(ACB\\) are similar",
        "Use \\(\\frac{MN}{x}=\\frac{5}{12}\\) and \\(NP=MC=12-x\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
